      "message": "I think we actually can\u0027t cache in those methods this way.\n\nSuppose we are deleting all the grants in a given domain_id. After that, querying for user_id and domain_id would return the cached values for the pair (user_id; domain_id).\n\nI suppose that\u0027s where your question come from, because that way we should check \u0027if user_id or domain_id:\u0027 instead of with an AND. However, how to know the other value (user or domain) to invalidate the cache, since the cache key is a pair user/domain ?\n\nThis can be solved if it\u0027s possible to invalidate all the cached valus where the keys match (*, domain_id), for example. I don\u0027t know if this library supports this.",
